WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back. Congrats on this.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.467
I want to get into all
this stuff.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.701
But first of all,
I want to know,

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.167
how are you liking
New York City?

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.400
-I'm loving it.
I always knew I wanted to live

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.601
in New York since I was
a little kid.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:10.767
-You did?

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.234
-Living here has been --
it's actually a dream.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.634
It's been amazing.
-And you have your apartment.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.968
What's the situation?
-Yeah, I fully moved here

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.901
I guess
a couple months ago officially.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.701
But I came with my cat, Dolly.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:26.701
I take her on walks
around the neighborhood.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:29.634
-How is Dolly?
Is she enjoying the city?

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:33.901
-She's adapting. She used to go
outside a lot on my patio.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:37.767
So, now I like to bring her
outside in a different way

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.868
because it's --
She's adapting to city life.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.334
-Well, how do you bring her out?
The cat would escape.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:47.300
-I got this little -- it's
almost like a suitcase,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.467
but it's clear and she sits in
there and goes around the block.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.934
-She looks like she's having
a great time.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.167
Can you zoom in on Dolly?

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:03.000
Uh, wow!

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.634
That is an unbelievable
invention.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.167
Never heard of that.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.634
I honestly think she doesn't
hate it.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.601
She seems to like it. Otherwise
I wouldn't bring her out in it.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.534
-She seems to like it?

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.033
-She's just looking around.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.934
[ Laughter ]
-She doesn't look happy at all.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:19.033
-Does she look pissed?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.434
-That's so funny.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.567
I want to talk about
"Little Shop of Horrors,"

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.434
one of my favorite musicals.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.501
And I got to know -- you were
telling me that you were

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:28.734
a musical theater nerd kid
when you were growing up.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.901
-Yes, I was.
-I have a picture of you.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.167
Explain this. How cute.
-Okay.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.367
-You're nine?

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.467
-This is me at "Rent."
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.968
-Okay.
-I don't remember exactly what

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:43.467
this production was but
Anthony Rapp and Adam Pascal,

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.968
the original cast members,
were doing the show.

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.133
I was a die-hard "Rent" fan at
such a young age.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.968
-Isn't it a little older --

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:56.133
-Yes, I don't know why my dad
really took me to the show.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.901
I was like, "Do you think they
thought that was weird?"

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.467
Yeah.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:01.968
-You just love the music?

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.901
-I love the music.
I kind of snuck away.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.601
My cousin was babysitting me.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.501
But I didn't know anything about
the show.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.434
I think I may have
just seen the disc,

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.634
and I watched it, and he didn't
stop me.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:14.534
-Did you understand what you
were watching?

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.601
-Not at all. No. Not at all.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.133
-I have another picture that
you brought,

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.334
and this is a Halloween parade.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:24.067
And you were dressed -- you were
dressed as Mimi from "Rent."

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:25.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.467
-In, like, third grade.
-This is third grade.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.200
Can you explain to everyone what
Mimi's character in "rent"?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.501
-Um, well, yeah, Mimi
is an exotic dancer.

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:36.667
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:38.667
Yeah, she is. Yeah.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.601
Did you know what that was?

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:43.467
Did you just think she danced
in exotic places?

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.534
-I don't know what my parents
were thinking

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.367
because they did let me go
like that.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.667
And my mom must have helped me
gather the costume.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.100
So, yeah.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.400
-Well, now here you are.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.300
You're starring as Audrey in
"Little Shop of Horrors."

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.133
This is fantastic.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:02.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.567
You started the show a couple
weeks ago, right?

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.400
How have the shows been
going so far?

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.033
-They've been great.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.868
I have really bad stage fright,
obviously.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:13.033
You can probably tell because
I'm freaking out right now.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.267
-No, you can't tell at all.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:20.267
-Mm. But I was so, so nervous
for the first show.

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:23.667
And then I did it in front of
the audience and I was kind of

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.801
relieved and felt good about
everything.

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:30.267
And then the second show, I
think I got a little cocky

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:32.968
and I sort of just, like -- I
was getting ready to

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:35.033
go on stage,
and I just walked on.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.734
And my first line in the show,

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.801
it's, "Good morning,
Mr. Mushnik."

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:42.400
And it just completely slipped
my mind.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.901
But, like, in a musical,
it doesn't stop moving.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:50.968
So I just sort of, like,
said, like...

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:54.501
-That's your opening line?

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:59.334
-And then I was sweating.
It derailed my entire show.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:02.467
-But now you're doing double --
you're doing on the weekends.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:05.834
-Yeah, but I can't get cocky.
I learned my lesson.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.133
-How many shows do you do
a week?

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.667
-Eight.
-Gosh.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.234
-Yeah.
-It's a lot of work.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.734
-But it's so fun.
I'm having the best time.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:16.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:18.400
-I saw on the socials that

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.434
a lot of famous people
are going to see you.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:21.634
Does it freak you out when

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:23.167
a famous person is
in the audience?

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.467
-Um, no.

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:27.067
They kind of keep asking,
though, like,

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:29.133
"Do you want us to tell you
if someone's here?"

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.634
-Do you want people to tell you?
-Yes.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:34.601
Because the theater is small,
and you can see everyone.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.968
So if someone randomly appeared
in the audience,

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:41.901
I think it would throw me if I
didn't know she was coming.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.467
-So you would just stare at
Kate Hudson the whole show?

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.567
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.267
-No one has freaked you out?
Kate Hudson you're fine with?

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:52.968
-Well, my favorite TV show is
"Catfish" on MTV.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.200
-Of course.
-I've watched every episode

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.267
multiple times.
-Nev?

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:01.000
-Nev from "Catfish" came,
and he came --

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.534
-He's the one that freaked you
out?

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.868
-I was freaking out that he came
and then he came back again

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:09.834
with his kids and he was sitting
in the second row.

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:11.501
And I was -- Yeah, I was dying.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.767
-That's the celebrity you were
like, "Oh, my gosh"?

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.033
-Yeah. I was not well.

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.000
-Wow.
-I was so excited.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.067
-Who is the actor that does
the voice of Audrey II?

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.367
-Oh, Aaron Harrington.
-It's his birthday today.

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.567
-It's his birthday today.
-I saw that 'cause he was

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:26.734
excited that you were
on the show tonight.

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:29.300
He's fantastic in the show.
-He's incredible.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.701
-Can we explain the show
for anyone

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:31.868
who hasn't seen
"Little Shop of Horrors"?

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:34.400
-Yeah. It's about a guy

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.434
who works at a flower shop on
Skid Row.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:42.901
And he finds this plant,
a fly trap.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.334
But we're not sure exactly
what it is.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:49.834
And the only way it can grow
is by eating humans.

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:51.534
-Yeah, yeah. It needs blood.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.400
-See, that's terrible.
It's not a great sell.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.200
-No, no. That's great.
-How would you say it?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.901
-That's exactly right. Yeah.

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:59.434
It's like a fly trap but --
-A man-eating plant.

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:02.300
-Yeah, it likes blood and then
starts eating humans

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:06.901
and starts eating everything and
grows to be giant and massive.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:09.767
-And it sort of destroys
its life.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:14.434
-Yes. But this is --
-It's a tragic tale.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:16.200
-I said, do you have
any superstitions?

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.334
And you said, yeah, you have to
touch the plant

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:20.968
before you go out.
-I know.

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:24.200
-Because it's a giant --
-It is giant.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.300
Before act two, at intermission,

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.567
I have to touch the plant's lips
with both hands.

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:31.968
I don't know how that started,

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:34.968
but now I really can't stop
doing it, yeah.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:36.868
I thought I was being slick
about it too,

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.334
and I don't think I am.

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.133
I think everyone is like, "Why
are you rubbing on the plant?"

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.067
[ Laughter ]
-"I need good luck.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:43.701
I need good luck on this."

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:46.534
Well, congrats.
It just got extended, your run.

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:49.501
-Yeah.
-This is going until April 30th.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:50.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
So, congratulations.

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:53.434
-Thank you.

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:57.367
-You were telling me that one of
your costars really is demanding

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.534
to be on the show here tonight.
-Yeah.

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:02.434
And I have to say yes.

00:07:02.434 --> 00:07:04.000
I mean, is she back there?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.634
[ Drum roll ]
Audrey II?

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:07.934
Come on out.

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:14.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.801
-Be careful.
-Oh, my God.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:20.567
-That's right, Jimmy, it's
Audrey II's time to shine.

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:24.300
It's my turn, Maude.
[ Laughs ]

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:28.734
-Audrey II, since you're here,

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:30.534
would you like to sing us
out to break?

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:32.934
-I thought you'd never ask.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:34.534
Hit it, Roots.

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:40.734
♪♪

00:07:40.734 --> 00:07:43.300
♪ If you want a rationale ♪

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.968
♪ It isn't very hard to see ♪

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:48.634
♪ Stop and think it over, pal ♪

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.133
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me ♪

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.934
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me ♪

00:07:54.000 --> 00:08:00.400
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me! ♪

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.300
-Maude Apatow, Audrey II,
everybody!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.434
Check out "Little Shop of
Horrors"

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:06.868
at the West Side Theater.

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:08.434
We'll be right back with
a performance

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:10.701
from Chance the Rapper.
Stick around.

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:13.267
-♪ If you want a rationale ♪

00:08:13.267 --> 00:08:15.934
♪ It isn't very hard to see ♪

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:18.267
♪ Stop and think it over, pal ♪

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:20.968
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me ♪

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.534
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me ♪

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:27.501
♪ The guy sure looks like
plant food to me! ♪

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:33.067
♪♪

00:08:33.067 --> 00:08:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

